--
N5008 [temp.spec.partial.order]/1 + [temp.func.order]: `traits<const
T*>` is more specialised than `traits<T*>` (the latter deduces from the
former, not vice versa; [temp.deduct.type]/8 makes cv part of the
pattern).  libstdc++'s iterator_traits<const char*> shape: choosing
`_Tp*` with `_Tp = const char` made value_type `const char`, so
std::regex's _Executor was instantiated over basic_regex<const char,
...> and matched no constructor.  Previously the pair tied on the
count heuristics and std::sort left the choice to candidate order.
